{"id":"91cc20dc3c0911ac","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-df-relativization.md","title":"Relativization","display":"df-relativization — Relativization","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-relativization","aliases":["58-df-relativization"],"display":"df-relativization — Relativization","depends_on":["[[58-df-formula]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-relativization"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-relativization</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-relativization — Relativization"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"58-df-formula\">58-df-formula</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\\in V\">\\(\\Sigma\\in V\\)</span> (signature)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi,\\psi,\\psi_1,\\psi_2\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\">\\(\\varphi,\\psi,\\psi_1,\\psi_2\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\">\\(x\\)</span> a variable, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"t_1,t_2\">\\(t_1,t_2\\)</span> terms</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R\">\\(R\\)</span> is an <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>-ary relation symbol of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\\in\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{rel}}\">\\(U\\in\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{rel}}\\)</span> is a designated unary relation symbol with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a_{\\mathrm{rel}}(U)=1\">\\(a_{\\mathrm{rel}}(U)=1\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U:\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\to\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\">\\(\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U:\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\to\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\)</span> (relativization operator defined recursively here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}relativization\\text{-}type}\\vdash U\\in\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{rel}}\\land a_{\\mathrm{rel}}(U)=1\\to\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U:\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\to\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}relativization\\text{-}type}\\vdash U\\in\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{rel}}\\land a_{\\mathrm{rel}}(U)=1\\to\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U:\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\to\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}relativization}\\vdash\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(t_1\\doteq t_2)&amp;\\coloneqq t_1\\doteq t_2,\\\\\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(R(t_1,\\ldots,t_n))&amp;\\coloneqq R(t_1,\\ldots,t_n),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\neg\\psi)&amp;\\coloneqq\\neg\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi_1\\lor\\psi_2)&amp;\\coloneqq\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi_1)\\lor\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi_2),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\forall x\\,\\psi)&amp;\\coloneqq\\forall x\\,(U(x)\\to\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi)).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}relativization}\\vdash\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(t_1\\doteq t_2)&amp;\\coloneqq t_1\\doteq t_2,\\\\\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(R(t_1,\\ldots,t_n))&amp;\\coloneqq R(t_1,\\ldots,t_n),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\neg\\psi)&amp;\\coloneqq\\neg\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi_1\\lor\\psi_2)&amp;\\coloneqq\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi_1)\\lor\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi_2),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\forall x\\,\\psi)&amp;\\coloneqq\\forall x\\,(U(x)\\to\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi)).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This is syntactic relativization to a unary predicate already present in the signature.  It therefore really maps <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span>-formulas to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span>-formulas instead of silently adjoining membership and a set parameter to an arbitrary language.</li>\n<li>To relativize a structure to a subset <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D\">\\(D\\)</span> of its universe, first expand the language by a fresh unary symbol <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\">\\(U\\)</span> interpreted as <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D\">\\(D\\)</span>; satisfaction in the restricted structure then agrees with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\varphi)\">\\(\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\varphi)\\)</span> under the usual closure hypotheses.</li>\n<li>The relative constructible hierarchy <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L[A]\">\\(L[A]\\)</span> is a different construction and is not conflated with quantifier relativization in this atom.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-formula]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\Sigma\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\varphi,\\psi,\\psi_1,\\psi_2\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)","display":false},{"tex":"x","display":false},{"tex":"t_1,t_2","display":false},{"tex":"R","display":false},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"\\Sigma","display":false},{"tex":"U\\in\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{rel}}","display":false},{"tex":"a_{\\mathrm{rel}}(U)=1","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U:\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\to\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}relativization\\text{-}type}\\vdash U\\in\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{rel}}\\land a_{\\mathrm{rel}}(U)=1\\to\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U:\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\to\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}relativization}\\vdash\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(t_1\\doteq t_2)&\\coloneqq t_1\\doteq t_2,\\\\\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(R(t_1,\\ldots,t_n))&\\coloneqq R(t_1,\\ldots,t_n),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\neg\\psi)&\\coloneqq\\neg\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi_1\\lor\\psi_2)&\\coloneqq\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi_1)\\lor\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi_2),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\forall x\\,\\psi)&\\coloneqq\\forall x\\,(U(x)\\to\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\psi)).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\Sigma","display":false},{"tex":"\\Sigma","display":false},{"tex":"D","display":false},{"tex":"U","display":false},{"tex":"D","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Rel}^{\\Sigma}_U(\\varphi)","display":false},{"tex":"L[A]","display":false}],"bytes":2115,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1069","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-relativization.md|58-df-relativization]]（batch19）"}],"outgoing":["65418b505fc53093"]}